{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1362880-where-is-zephyr-and-the-cynosure-coast","id":1362880,"title":"Where is Zephyr and the Cynosure Coast?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-01-23T07:19:36-08:00","id":1362880,"title":"Where is Zephyr and the Cynosure Coast?","content":"I've been trying to figure out where Zephyr and Cynosure Coast regions are in Creation. At the moment, I'm assuming that it's location is &quot;Where you need it to be for your story, within reason&quot; since the details we have are rather sparse. But before I plop it down on the map, I wanted to be sure I wasn't missing anything that would conflict with my intended placement.<br /> <br /> Based on the scattered descriptions we have for these regions, I want to place it north of An-Teng. The headwaters of the Elidad would be in the northern Firepeaks, flowing south-by-southwest toward the ocean. The proximity of this region to shipping lanes linking the Inner Sea to the Great Western Ocean would help explain why the Cynosure Coast's city-states are said to be so wealthy. <br /> <br /> The one thing that gives me pause here is the description of Ketzepah Narrow-Ways and her horde &quot;emerging from the Southern desert&quot; to invade Zephyr, as that makes it seem like the Burning Sands should be closer than it would be if Zephyr is on the western side of the Firepeaks. But I suppose Ketzepah and company could emerge from the deserts and travel some mountain passes to reach their destination.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2118-reminiscent-oasis","name":"Reminiscent Oasis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2118_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"158"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-23T07:49:27-08:00","id":1362887,"title":"","content":"Zephyr is roughly equidistant between the Lap and Paragon. The Cynosure Coast is along the bay west of Paragon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-23T08:02:58-08:00","id":1362889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1362880-where-is-zephyr-and-the-cynosure-coast?p=1362887#post1362887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Zephyr is roughly equidistant between the Lap and Paragon. The Cynosure Coast is along the bay west of Paragon.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was my second option. On the bright side, that puts it more in the immediate area that my game will be focusing on, though I was looking forward to having something significant in that area north of An-Teng.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2118-reminiscent-oasis","name":"Reminiscent Oasis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2118_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"158"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-26T09:41:00-08:00","id":1363465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reminiscent Oasis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1362880-where-is-zephyr-and-the-cynosure-coast?p=1362889#post1362889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That was my second option. On the bright side, that puts it more in the immediate area that my game will be focusing on, though I was looking forward to having something significant in that area north of An-Teng.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You may, if want to create it. If you want already existing stuff, maybe re-reading bits of Blood &amp; Salt or CoTD: South might get you some juicy tidbits about the area to work with.<br /> <br /> Also, take a look at CoCD: Yu-Shan and if any of the gates might be there or close by, they always come with some background bits/plot hooks for a ST to tinker with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-27T00:19:10-08:00","id":1363567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1362880-where-is-zephyr-and-the-cynosure-coast?p=1363465#post1363465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> You may, if want to create it. If you want already existing stuff, maybe re-reading bits of Blood &amp; Salt or CoTD: South might get you some juicy tidbits about the area to work with.<br /> <br /> Also, take a look at CoCD: Yu-Shan and if any of the gates might be there or close by, they always come with some background bits/plot hooks for a ST to tinker with.</div> </div> </div> </div>I may end up doing something with the area. CoTD: South doesn't appear to have anything on it, and while there is a Gate in the area, information provided in Yu-Shan is only &quot;250 northeast of An-Teng, this gateway is used by many of the regional gods to go to and from Heaven.&quot; <br /> <br /> In any case, the group decided to start in Chiaroscuro, so it'll be a while before I need to start filling in that blank slate. If I need to at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2118-reminiscent-oasis","name":"Reminiscent Oasis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2118_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"158"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-28T04:31:46-08:00","id":1363769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reminiscent Oasis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1362880-where-is-zephyr-and-the-cynosure-coast?p=1363567#post1363567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I may end up doing something with the area. CoTD: South doesn't appear to have anything on it,</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It doesn't help that sometimes it seems like whoever edited CoTD: South thought of maps as art more than tools to convey information about places for direct use in the table and kind of feels like you have to wrestle the book to relate chapter info and their actual locations....<br /> <br /> In CoTD: South i found mention of a Sualin, &quot;the self-styled Diamond Mandarin of a neighboring kingdom&quot; that invaded the seemingly defenseless country when the Empress withdrew An-Teng\u2019s garrison to fight in the war against the Anathema Jochim (RY 578-585), leading to 2 years of war and 1 of sovereignity for An-Teng's monarchs, at least until the Dynasts defeated Jochim and came back. There's no more on Sualin or where its kingdom was located or not, but thought it worth to mention.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reminiscent Oasis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1362880-where-is-zephyr-and-the-cynosure-coast?p=1363567#post1363567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> and while there is a Gate in the area, information provided in Yu-Shan is only &quot;250 northeast of An-Teng, this gateway is used by many of the regional gods to go to and from Heaven.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Just our luck, to get the one gateway out of sixty with bland writing and no hooks, eh?<br /> <br /> That said, it <b>does </b>mean that gate sees considerable traffic, what is <b>not </b>universally the case, might be said (surprising as it may be, as we are speaking of 60 passages <i>to span the whole of Creation</i>), if memory tricks me not. And if sees much traffic is probably because there are major populations to worship them or some other major attractive in the Fire Plains region (area's name, at least among visitors from heaven, if the gates' table from page 81 serves as an indicator).<br /> <br /> The fact that the portal in the Yu-Shan side is located in the Pangaean District, an area of the celestial city made up largely of hilly terrain and rivers with the occasional canal from the centers crossing, might also make the southern gateways as a whole great places for deities to act in ways that might be seen as irregular by celestial authorities.<br /> <br /> Also relatively close, we have this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CoCD:Yu-shan, pg. 112-113</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gateway 48 [<b><i>Hurricane Gate</i></b>]: 250 miles east of Nightfall Island, there is a pirate\u2019s cove utilized by many of the bandits in the area. It is effectively a small city of what amounts to a sandbar supporting acres of docks, where anything is for sale and everything is permitted, ruled by a coalition of the stronger buccaneers. The area once was used as something of a brothel by gods within Yu-Shan looking to experience the seamier side of life in Creation, so a handful of God-Blooded hold various ranks in pirate crews. Their parents are aware of their activities, and while they do nothing to condone it, the gods would hate to see something happen to their offspring. Given the higher rate of God-Bloods within the population, the Realm\u2019s skeleton merchant-marine fleet has taken an interest in the predations of the local pirates, and skirmishes have become more frequent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good? It can get better, as pretty much the same place is identified as <i><b>Whale Bay</b></i> in pages 83-85 of CoCD: Underworld.<br /> No major shadowlands for the isle are mentioned, but that is what STs and plot hooks are for, no? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Incidentally, some of the terms in which their relationship with Stygia and the West are described made me think a little of a proto-Wu-Jian, though the location is completely different and Whale Bay more haggard and less bustling/bursting with people.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exalted 3e, pg. 7</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Wu-Jian began in the first days, nearly the very first days, as the outcast islands.<br /> They roamed free. They swum like a pod of whales playing in the ocean.<br /> They knew no stability and no order. They drifted on the currents and the waves.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>What if Whale Bay was named so not for some beached ghostly beast carcass, but being the one that ran away, the escaped child/sibling of the pod of islands of the first days? Hmmm.....<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reminiscent Oasis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1362880-where-is-zephyr-and-the-cynosure-coast?p=1363567#post1363567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In any case, the group decided to start in Chiaroscuro, so it'll be a while before I need to start filling in that blank slate. If I need to at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh well, then i guess An-Teng and its neighboring area gets to the wayside. It happens, but considering there's a bunch of fluff on Chiaroscuro i guess you'll have plenty to toy and tinker with (if your Sanguine Saber thread serves as indicator).<br /> <br /> As an aside, there's a Yu-shan gate in the city - in Grandmother Bright's neighborhood. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 01-28-2020, 09:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}